virglrenderer: vrend on macOS over ANGLE (GLES on Metal).
Cherry-picked from utmapp/virglrenderer (MIT, UTM's fork) 5d26f605f50f8e22002ec6db5fb775e1992d4e96:
- ANGLE/GLES fixes (texture max level, GLSL ES version, integer vertex attributes, CLEAR_TEXTURE,
  CLAMP_TO_BORDER fallback, draw_elements_base_vertex detection, missing glTexBuffer);
- Metal textures exported/imported through shared memory and EGL_ANGLE_metal images,
  virgl_renderer_create_handle_for_scanout (a Metal texture for a scanout resource),
  direct BGRA uploads for externally-backed resources on GLES.
Local: vrend's own EGL winsys without GBM (the default display: ANGLE's Metal display), so the
embedder needs no GL callbacks (VIRGL_RENDERER_USE_EGL | VIRGL_RENDERER_USE_GLES).

  e12d278d osy: vrend: do not set GL_TEXTURE_MAX_LEVEL to 0
  e37431a7 Akihiko Odaki: vrend: Relax the GLSL ES version requirement
  9c7e6a09 Akihiko Odaki: vrend: Use integer vertex attribute on ANGLE on Apple
  ccd003cd Akihiko Odaki: vrend: Reject VIRGL_CCMD_CLEAR_TEXTURE if unsupported
  69ef550e Akihiko Odaki: vrend: Implement fallback for GL_CLAMP_TO_BORDER
  55cf1931 osy: vrend: detect missing feat_draw_elements_base_vertex
  f71d0c1b osy: vrend: avoid crashing when glTexBuffer is not implemented
  bdda5ac7 osy: vrend: export and import Metal textures via shared memory
  0f5cb82d osy: virglrenderer: add virgl_renderer_create_handle_for_scanout
  d8add9ac osy: vrend: upload bgra directly for externally-backed resources on GLES
  36b458f3 x: vrend: own EGL winsys without GBM (the default display, e.g. ANGLE on macOS)

